# Internationalization (i18n) Guide

## Overview
DECM uses [react-i18next](https://react.i18next.com/) for internationalization, supporting multiple languages with type-safe translations.

## Supported Languages
- **English (en)** - Default language 🇬🇧
- **Thai (th)** - Thai language 🇹🇭

## Configuration Files
- Config: [apps/web/src/lib/i18n/config.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/i18n/config.ts)
- English translations: [apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json)
- Thai translations: [apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/th.json](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/th.json)
- Type definitions: [apps/web/src/lib/i18n/types.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/i18n/types.ts)

## Basic Usage

### Import and Use
```tsx
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

export const MyComponent = () => {
    const { t } = useTranslation();
    
    return (
        <div>
            <h1>{t('common.welcome')}</h1>
            <p>{t('home.hero.subtitle')}</p>
        </div>
    );
};
```

### With Typography Component
```tsx
import { Typography } from '@/components/typography/typography';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

export const MyComponent = () => {
    const { t } = useTranslation();
    
    return (
        <Typography variant="header" tag="h1">
            {t('page.title')}
        </Typography>
    );
};
```

## Translation File Structure

### Namespace Organization
```json
{
    "common": {
        "appName": "DECM",
        "welcome": "Welcome",
        "loading": "Loading..."
    },
    "auth": {
        "signIn": "Sign In",
        "signUp": "Sign Up"
    },
    "oauth": {
        "google": {
            "title": "Authenticating with Google",
            "subtitle": "Please wait while we verify your account"
        }
    }
}
```

### Key Naming Convention
Use dot notation for nested keys:
- `common.welcome` → "Welcome"
- `auth.signIn` → "Sign In"
- `oauth.google.title` → "Authenticating with Google"

## Adding New Translations

### Step 1: Add to Translation Files

**English** (`apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json`):
```json
{
    "myFeature": {
        "title": "My Feature",
        "description": "This is a description",
        "action": "Click here"
    }
}
```

**Thai** (`apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/th.json`):
```json
{
    "myFeature": {
        "title": "ฟีเจอร์ของฉัน",
        "description": "นี่คือคำอธิบาย",
        "action": "คลิกที่นี่"
    }
}
```

### Step 2: Use in Components
```tsx
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';
import { Typography } from '@/components/typography/typography';

export const MyFeature = () => {
    const { t } = useTranslation();
    
    return (
        <div>
            <Typography variant="header" tag="h2">
                {t('myFeature.title')}
            </Typography>
            <Typography variant="text" tag="p">
                {t('myFeature.description')}
            </Typography>
            <button>{t('myFeature.action')}</button>
        </div>
    );
};
```

## Common Translation Namespaces

### 1. Common
Global, reusable translations:
```tsx
t('common.loading')      // "Loading..."
t('common.error')        // "Error"
t('common.success')      // "Success"
t('common.save')         // "Save"
t('common.cancel')       // "Cancel"
t('common.appName')      // "DECM"
```

### 2. Navigation
Navigation-related text:
```tsx
t('nav.home')           // "Home"
t('nav.events')         // "Events"
t('nav.profile')        // "Profile"
t('nav.signIn')         // "Sign In"
```

### 3. Authentication
Auth-related text:
```tsx
t('auth.signIn')                // "Sign In"
t('auth.signUp')                // "Sign Up"
t('auth.walletConnect')         // "Connect Wallet"
t('auth.googleLogin')           // "Continue with Google"
t('auth.email')                 // "Email"
t('auth.password')              // "Password"
```

### 4. OAuth
OAuth process text:
```tsx
t('oauth.google.title')         // "Authenticating with Google"
t('oauth.google.subtitle')      // "Please wait while we verify..."
t('oauth.google.processing')    // "Processing..."
```

### 5. Errors
Error messages:
```tsx
t('errors.generic')             // "Something went wrong..."
t('errors.network')             // "Network error..."
t('errors.unauthorized')        // "You are not authorized..."
```

### 6. Validation
Form validation messages:
```tsx
t('validation.required')        // "This field is required"
t('validation.invalidEmail')    // "Invalid email address"
t('validation.passwordTooShort') // "Password must be..."
```

## Advanced Features

### 1. Interpolation
Use variables in translations:

**Translation file:**
```json
{
    "greeting": "Welcome, {{name}}!",
    "itemCount": "You have {{count}} items"
}
```

**Component:**
```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation();

t('greeting', { name: 'John' })           // "Welcome, John!"
t('itemCount', { count: 5 })              // "You have 5 items"
```

### 2. Pluralization
Handle singular/plural forms:

**Translation file:**
```json
{
    "items": "{{count}} item",
    "items_plural": "{{count}} items"
}
```

**Component:**
```tsx
t('items', { count: 1 })    // "1 item"
t('items', { count: 5 })    // "5 items"
```

### 3. Accessing i18n Instance
For more control:

```tsx
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

export const LanguageInfo = () => {
    const { t, i18n } = useTranslation();
    
    const changeLanguage = (lng: string) => {
        i18n.changeLanguage(lng);
    };
    
    return (
        <div>
            <p>Current: {i18n.language}</p>
            <button onClick={() => changeLanguage('th')}>
                Switch to Thai
            </button>
        </div>
    );
};
```

### 4. In Helmet/Metadata
Use translations in page metadata:

```tsx
import { FaviconHelmet } from '@/components/providers/helmets/FaviconHelmet';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

const MyPage = () => {
    const { t } = useTranslation();
    
    return (
        <>
            <FaviconHelmet
                title={`${t('page.title')} | ${t('common.appName')}`}
                description={t('page.description')}
            />
            <MyPageContent />
        </>
    );
};
```

